  {
   "cards": [
    {
     "front": "How many rows in a truth table with 4 variables?",
     "back": "2^4 = **16** rows — one per assignment."
    },
    {
     "front": "State De Morgan's law for AND.",
     "back": "NOT (p AND q) = (NOT p) OR (NOT q) — verified on all 4 rows."
    },
    {
     "front": "State De Morgan's law for OR.",
     "back": "NOT (p OR q) = (NOT p) AND (NOT q)."
    },
    {
     "front": "Define p -> q without using ->.",
     "back": "(NOT p) OR q. Only false when p=T, q=F."
    },
    {
     "front": "What is the contrapositive of p -> q?",
     "back": "(NOT q) -> (NOT p) — logically equivalent to the original."
    },
    {
     "front": "Is the converse of p -> q equivalent to p -> q?",
     "back": "No. Counterexample: p=T, q=F makes p->q false but q->p true."
    },
    {
     "front": "Absorption law?",
     "back": "p OR (p AND q) = p; p AND (p OR q) = p."
    },
    {
     "front": "What does EXISTS x, P(x) require over a finite domain?",
     "back": "At least one domain element making P true — a single witness."
    },
    {
     "front": "What does FORALL x, P(x) require?",
     "back": "Every domain element makes P true — one counterexample falsifies it."
    },
    {
     "front": "Simplify (a AND b) OR (a AND NOT b).",
     "back": "a — factor to a AND (b OR NOT b) = a AND T."
    },
    {
     "front": "Order of evaluation in (p AND q) OR (NOT r)?",
     "back": "Parentheses, then NOT, then AND, then OR — inside-out."
    },
    {
     "front": "Evaluate (T AND F) OR (NOT T).",
     "back": "(F) OR (F) = **F**."
    }
   ],
   "code": "IL-14",
   "crossLinks": [],
   "drills": [
    {
     "title": "Logic evaluation sprint",
     "items": [
      {
       "prompt": "Evaluate (T OR F) AND (NOT F).",
       "answer": "T",
       "explain": "(T OR F)=T; NOT F=T; T AND T=T."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "Evaluate NOT (T AND T) OR F.",
       "answer": "F",
       "explain": "NOT(T AND T)=F; F OR F=F. NOT binds tightest."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "p=F, q=F. Evaluate (NOT p) -> q.",
       "answer": "F",
       "explain": "(NOT F)=T; T -> F is the one false case of implication."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "How many assignments falsify (p AND q) OR (p AND NOT q)?",
       "answer": "2 of 4",
       "explain": "The expression simplifies to p; falsified exactly when p=F (2 rows)."
      }
     ],
     "id": "il-14-sre-devops-cloud-security-interview-prep-math-logic--drill-1"
    },
    {
     "title": "Equivalence proofs",
     "items": [
      {
       "prompt": "Prove NOT (p OR q) = (NOT p) AND (NOT q) by cases.",
       "answer": "All 4 rows agree",
       "explain": "Enumerate (T,T),(T,F),(F,T),(F,F): both sides match on every row — De Morgan verified."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "Is (p -> q) equivalent to (NOT p) -> (NOT q)? Justify.",
       "answer": "No",
       "explain": "Counterexample p=T,q=T: original true, inverse (F->F) true... use p=F,q=T: original true, inverse (T->F) false. Not equivalent."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "Simplify (x OR y) AND (x OR NOT y) AND (NOT x OR y).",
       "answer": "x AND y",
       "explain": "First two factor to x; x AND ((NOT x) OR y) absorbs to x AND y."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "Translate 'every admin has MFA' into quantifiers.",
       "answer": "FORALL u, (admin(u) -> mfa(u))",
       "explain": "Universal over users; implication inside captures 'if admin then MFA'."
      }
     ],
     "id": "il-14-sre-devops-cloud-security-interview-prep-math-logic--drill-2"
    }
   ],
   "estimatedMinutes": 345,
   "handsOnLab": {
    "title": "Verify logic laws in Python",
    "brief": "You will write a brute-force truth-table checker in Python and use it to verify De Morgan's laws, the contrapositive, and absorption — replacing hand-waving with enumeration.",
    "steps": [
     "Write a function tt(vars, fn) that iterates over all 2^n assignments using itertools.product and returns the table.",
     "Use it to print the full truth table of (p -> q), defined as (not p) or q.",
     "Verify De Morgan: assert all rows agree for NOT(p AND q) vs (NOT p) OR (NOT q).",
     "Verify the contrapositive: assert (p->q) matches ((not q) -> (not p)) on all rows, and find the counterexample row for the converse.",
     "Verify absorption p OR (p AND q) == p on all 8 rows of (p,q,r) — extra variable included to prove irrelevance.",
     "Write verify_equiv(f, g, vars) and use it to check two simplifications of your own invention."
    ],
