      },
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: How do you present architecture tradeoffs without rambling?",
       "answer": "Three beats per decision: the choice, what it costs (money, complexity, latency), and when you'd choose differently. Then stop and invite the follow-up. The interview line: 'every architecture is a list of paid prices — I show the receipts.'",
       "explain": "Core recall for this module. If this wasn't fluent, re-read the 'Concepts' note and retry until it is."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: How do you present a costed architecture honestly?",
