     "id": "security-eng-interview-prep--sec-crypto--drill-recall",
     "title": "Recall sprint: Cryptography in Practice",
     "items": [
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: What does ‘randomness done right’ mean?",
       "answer": "Cryptographic randomness (CSPRNG: /dev/urandom, secrets module) for keys, tokens, and nonces — never Math.random() or seeded PRNGs for security purposes. The interview line: ‘predictable randomness is no randomness.’",
       "explain": "Core recall for this module. If this wasn't fluent, re-read the 'Concepts' note and retry until it is."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: How do you answer 'should we encrypt it twice for safety'?",
       "answer": "With the threat model: double encryption adds complexity and key-management burden for marginal gain — the risk is almost never the cipher, it's the keys, the randomness, and the implementation. Fix the key management first. The interview line: 'I don't armor the vault door while the keys hang on a hook beside it.'",
       "explain": "Core recall for this module. If this wasn't fluent, re-read the 'Concepts' note and retry until it is."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: How do you discuss hashing vs encryption for passwords?",
       "answer": "Hashing is one-way (verification without recovery); encryption is reversible (a breached key exposes all). The interview line: ‘passwords are verified, never decrypted.’",
       "explain": "Core recall for this module. If this wasn't fluent, re-read the 'Concepts' note and retry until it is."
      },
      {
       "prompt": "From memory, in one or two sentences: What do interviewers probe in forward secrecy?",
       "answer": "Ephemeral key exchange (ECDHE) so a future key compromise can’t decrypt past traffic. The interview line: ‘forward secrecy bounds the blast radius of a stolen key.’",
       "explain": "Core recall for this module. If this wasn't fluent, re-read the 'Concepts' note and retry until it is."
      }
     ]
    },
